%I A226918 #20 Aug 22 2026 10:03:05
%S A226918 0,0,3,4,5,7,9,13,16,20,24,28
%N A226918 Minimal number of 1X3 I-trominoes needed to prevent any further I-tromino from being placed on an n X n grid.
%C A226918 The I-trominoes must line up with the squares on the grid and must occupy exactly three squares (skew placements are not allowed).
%C A226918 a(n) is the independent domination number of a graph with one node per tromino and an edge for each pair of trominoes that conflict. - _Rob Pratt_, Oct 02 2019
%H A226918 Juris Cernenoks and Andrejs Cibulis, <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20150911053519/http://aict.itf.llu.lv/files/rakstkraj/2013/Cernenoks_AICT2013.pdf">Application of IT in Mathematical Proofs and in Checking of Results of Pupils' Research</a>, Int'l Conf. Appl. Info. Commun. Tech. (Jelgava, Latvia, AICT2013, April 2013), 25-26.
%H A226918 Juris Cernenoks and Andrejs Cibulis, <a href="/A226918/a226918.jpg">Illustration of initial terms</a> (Figure 11 from the above reference, included with permission of the authors).
%K A226918 nonn,more,changed
